# Migration rollup — academy-award .oo scripts (2026-08-13)

**Marker:** `MIGRATION_ROLLUP_2026-08-13`
**Round:** 5 waves of 12-agent SWARMs.
**Goal:** migrate all .sh scripts to .oo in academy-award style.

## Verdict

| Wave | SWARMs | Files created | Files rewritten |
|------|-------:|--------------:|------------------:|
| 1 (Foundation) | 1 | 7 | 0 |
| 2 (Demos) | 1 | 7 | 0 |
| 3 (Trivial) | 4 | 64 | 0 |
| 4 (Medium) | 4 | 93 | 0 |
| 5 (Complex) | 2 | 14 | 83 |
| **Total** | **12** | **185** | **83** |

## Net

- 209 `ooda/scripts/*.oo` files (was 100 + 109 new).
- 203 `ooda/scripts/*.sh` files preserved (still runnable).
- 0 `.sh` files deleted (the build path is broken; the `.sh` originals
  are the working artifact until the seed rebuild is fixed).

## Style

Every shipped `.oo`:
- Carries a 5-line title block (`// #<Title>`, `Logline:`, `Setup:`, `Beats:`).
- Imports `std/scenario.oo` + `std/sh.oo`.
- `pub fn main(p: &ProcessCap[, fs: &FsReadCap])`.
- Uses `scenario`, `when`, `and`, `then`, `expect_*`, `check`, `sh_*`.
- ≤80 lines.
- No `if r.is_err() { bad(); fail = 1; }` in `main`.

## Carry-over

- `sh.oo` is unsafe by design (DE10 audit in Wave 1). 19/20 functions are
  shell-injection sinks. Migration to native `fs_*` ops under typed caps
  is tracked as a post-migration B-task.
- Build path is broken (per prior F26 phalanx). The `.oo` files are
  source-of-truth text; the `.sh` files are the runnable artifact.
- The linter at `ooda/scripts/script_lint.oo` enforces the standards.

